  "findings": [
    "Full original Say plus actual CRT RTTI and non-High process virtuals returns success 1/duration 0 in 384 cases without entering RNG/INFO/conditions. Only argument extraction is supplied. The first thread-fixture failure and opaque parameter-pointer correction remain recorded.",
    "All Low/MiddleLow/MiddleHigh process vtables use 5E17C0 RET20 as their speech dispatcher. Actual High dispatch 62A9C0 is separate and outside this proof.",
    "The shipped MS48 stage 70 result explicitly addresses native actor 028A7A and topic GOODBYE (0000D4). The prison course has no resident speaker Ptr for that reference. The original non-High result is zero, so inventing a voice by evaluating candidates is incorrect.",
    "ScriptManager now returns double0 for Say with an empty speaker Ptr and a known typed native ActorCharacter/ActorCreature reference. Nonactor voice overrides and SayTo are not blanket-skipped. No actor authority, INFO result or speech queue is created.",
    "The actual-store test supplies a real random INFO candidate: cold NPC/Creature calls return0 without actor state or RNG changes; resident NPC/Creature calls still reach the candidate and draw twice before empty VFS stops audio.",
    "Both full engine inventories pass 1,858 tests. The stage-gated real-script course now passes all existing command/audio/weather/save checks plus explicit remote zero trace and absence of a null-speaker dialogue lookup. The generated mixed audio is valid non-silent 48kHz stereo float WAVE; this does not isolate voice samples."
  ],
  "limits": [
    "The host rule is a necessary no-resident-actor gate, not a complete mapping of all materialized process tiers. Native High speech, nonactor voice overrides, and all SayTo options have separate open work.",
    "Native oracle scope supplies command arguments and fixture fields. No compiled original-script parsing, real original-game input or actual High-process audio is claimed.",
    "The real course still reports vanilla numeric and uninitialized-actor command diagnostics, enumerated in this receipt; passing the bounded command/audio checks is not error-free general gameplay.",
    "Prior startup and audio failures remain retained. No arbitrary missing-speaker fallback, forced actor activation or weakened expected command check was used.",
    "Automatic common-hit speech/resource/condition preparation/publication, root quest predicate authority, INFO history/results and complete S4 combat input/restart acceptance remain open.",
    "Sanitizer leak detection disabled. The audio inspection validates the mixed output and format/levels only."
  ]
}
